completionSummary:
Protected VS Code now admits a daemon only if a fresh /health?challenge answer matches the HMAC of a key this extension minted. The key goes into the installed daemon's env (MOE_SPAWN_PROOF_KEY) and is kept in the session map plus the owner-only store (kind 'spawn', read only from a root outside the project). Everything else gets the fixed refusal and no WebSocket: daemon.json, /health identity, a configured endpoint, untrusted/malformed/stale records, timeouts. Replace is offered only for a daemon.json daemon with a valid pid, via a modal whose only action is Stop and Replace. It runs the installed CLI stop (20 s; only its own child is killed), waits 15 s/250 ms for the pid and metadata to clear, then does a fresh spawn and re-admission. LEGACY is unchanged.
Review fixes this session, RED-checked:
- pid text shown only for a positive integer (daemon.json is repo text);
- workspace captured before the identity probe (a mid-probe switch to legacy bypassed the gate);
- a final refusal suppresses auto-reconnect (JetBrains no-retry, so no modal re-pops);
- record daemon key via projectStateKey.
Third-file disclosure (comment-d4217a23, amend-1): tests/protected-daemon-spawn.test.cjs +5/-2. D1 adds a 64-hex MOE_SPAWN_PROOF_KEY to the exact env, and both ENOENT-after-cancel tests cancel at the stub spawn, still with 1 spawn. No other existing test changed. Size from b4cfae12: +454/-9, net 445 of 520 (prop-35eadcbd, pending).
